(1949102, 265546, 44490, '<td valign="top">Too blatant for some, too obscure for others, oh well...  For those who missed it -- have you ever had to feed a parking meter, only to find that you didn''t have any change?  So you had to buy a pack of gum just to get change, and by that time, the meter "person" had already given you a ticket.<br/> <br/>By the way, I tried other angles and compositions, but there are limits to where you can position your car.  I also couldn''t get the red "expired" sign, as it is only on the side facing the street.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments, sorry it isn''t studio quality, but I think that the best part of dpchallenge is that it encourages me to get out and enjoy shooting while thinking more creatively.  I hope that we can all encourage each other to participate and practice, and thanks to all for the variety of ideas and images.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-12-14 00:32:59.</i></td>', 'Too blatant for some, too obscure for others, oh well...  For those who missed it -- have you ever had to feed a parking meter, only to find that you didn''t have any change?  So you had to buy a pack of gum just to get change, and by that time, the meter "person" had already given you a ticket. By the way, I tried other angles and compositions, but there are limits to where you can position your car.  I also couldn''t get the red "expired" sign, as it is only on the side facing the street. Thanks for the comments, sorry it isn''t studio quality, but I think that the best part of dpchallenge is that it encourages me to get out and enjoy shooting while thinking more creatively.  I hope that we can all encourage each other to participate and practice, and thanks to all for the variety of ideas and images.', '2005-12-14 00:28:48.000000', '2005-12-14 00:32:59.000000', 0),
